{"name":"Bonfire Night","hex":"#de6a41","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bonfire Night","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Synonym of Guy Fawkes Night.","Synonym of Eleventh Night (“night before 12 July”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bonfire_Night"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bonfire Night","blocks":[{"text":"Bonfire Night is a name given to various yearly events marked by bonfires and fireworks. These include Guy Fawkes Night in Great Britain; All Hallows' Eve ; May Eve ; Midsummer Eve/Saint John's Eve ; the Eleventh Night among Northern Ireland Protestants; and the Feast of the Assumption among Northern Ireland Catholics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Bonfire_on_Mississippi_River_levee_St._James_Parish_Louisiana.jpg/330px-Bonfire_on_Mississippi_River_levee_St._James_Parish_Louisiana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonfire_Night","wikidata":"Q4941792"},{"title":"Bonfire","blocks":[{"text":"A bonfire is a large and controlled outdoor fire, used for waste disposal or as part of a religious feast, such as Saint John's Eve."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Seurasaari-2005-johannus2.jpg/330px-Seurasaari-2005-johannus2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonfire","wikidata":"Q9505308"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Bonfire_on_Mississippi_River_levee_St._James_Parish_Louisiana.jpg/500px-Bonfire_on_Mississippi_River_levee_St._James_Parish_Louisiana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Bonfire_on_Mississippi_River_levee_St._James_Parish_Louisiana.jpg/500px-Bonfire_on_Mississippi_River_levee_St._James_Parish_Louisiana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Christmas Eve celebration bonfire in Louisiana, United States","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABonfire_on_Mississippi_River_levee_St._James_Parish_Louisiana.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg/500px-Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg/1280px-Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg/500px-Worcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fireworks display at a park in Worcestershire, United Kingdom","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWorcs_Fireworks_2025.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Seurasaari-2005-johannus2.jpg/500px-Seurasaari-2005-johannus2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Seurasaari-2005-johannus2